strReplace [SimTalk]
Searches for the text you specified as the TextToFind within the string SourceText and replaces all
occurrences with the text you specified as the string ReplaceBy. The function returns the resulting string.
Type
Function
Syntax
strReplace(SourceText:string, TextToFind:string, ReplaceBy:string) -> string
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter SourceText of data type string designates the source text within which you want to
search.
• The parameter TextToFind of data type string designates the text which you want to find.
• The parameter ReplaceBy of data type string designates the text which is going to replace the text you
are searching for in all occurrences, which it found.
Return Value
The return value has the data type string.
Plant Simulation does not modify the SourceText during and after the search.
Example
var SourceText : string := "hello world"
var Result1 : string := strReplace(SourceText, "l", "XY") -- returns 
"heXYXYo worXYd"
var Result2 : string := strReplace(SourceText, "ll", "x") -- returns "hexo 
world"
var Result3 : string := strReplace(SourceText, "L", "x")  -- returns "hello 
world" because upper-case L is not contained
strReplace [SimTalk]
12-342 Plant Simulation Help
